{
  "id": 975,
  "description": "# 🪓⛏️🎣 **welcome!** 🧪🔥🍖\nWe are a guild for Combat Level 1 Skillers only.\n\n###### &quot;Masters of discipline whose hands remain untarnished by the stains of raid and combat&quot;\n\n#### Contents:\n1. Guild showcase\n2. Guild goals\n3. Read before you apply\n4. Skiller tips &amp; ideas\n\n###### Last updated: Oct 2026\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n## 1. ✨️ __guild showcase__\nSkill Mastery Badges\n###### Every time a guild member reaches level 100 in a skill, their Mastery Badge is added to this showcase.\n\n# 🐕 ⛏️ ⛏️ ⛏️ 🔥 🪓 🪓 🪓 🎣 🎣 🎣 🎣 🍖 🍖 🍖 🍖 🍖 🎯 🎯 🏠 🏠 🏠 🧪\n\nMiscellaneous Guild Stats:\n- Badges collected: 23\n- Completionist progress: 9/22\n- Total total level: 10,467\n- Total ascension level: 148\n- Mythic tools acquired: 2\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n## 2. 👑 __guild goals__\n- Level 70 Guild for Energizing Pool (earned solely through completing challenges)\n- Guild achievements list\n- Guild skill mastery completionist status (collectively obtain every possible non-combat badge across all guild members)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n## 3. 📜 __read before you apply__\nValid applicants must have the following:\n1. ⚔️ Combat Level 1\n2. 📊 Total Level 200+\n3. 🎁 Contribute 500+ items toward guild Challenges within 1 week of joining\n\nGuidelines to know:\n- ⚔️ Levelling-up your Combat skill will remove you from the guild.\n- 🚫 Applications from Characters with a Combat level of 2 or higher will not be accepted. Applications from Characters who have used a ♻️ Reset Stone on their Combat skill will also not be accepted.\n- 🏰 Guild Mastery EXP and Guild EXP are earned solely through completing Challenges. Stockpile contributions are welcomed but not required.\n- 🔁 Trade-locked classes will be unable to participate in guild Challenges &amp; Stockpile contribution. Join a banished guild instead to enjoy these functions with fellow trade-locked classes.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n## 4. 🧩 __skiller tips &amp; ideas__\nMoney-Making Tips\n- (1M+ gold/mo) Fish and Cook on your alternate characters and trade the profits to your main character. This is a reliable method for sustaining membership via in-game funds.\n- Mining and selling coal is an early, easy access way to earn steady gold.\n- The higher your Bartering level, the more gold you earn from selling items to the Vendor. At high levels, this can make some skilling methods instantly profitable that are normally unprofitable (such as Alchemy).\n\nGeneral Tips\n- Check out the Shooting Star location thread in the Tavern for easy tracking of some of the best temporary EXP/eff boosts.\n- Use Alchemy crystals for temporary skilling boosts that can significantly increase EXP/eff for often only a small price.\n- more coming soon",
